(6844858, 1029170, 123348, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by CNovack:</b></div><hr/><i> Voted earlier coming back to comment.<br/> <br/>Nice candid street photo. I like how you captured his beaming smile. However, I do wish that you captured more of what was ocurring on the left side of the frame to tell the story of what he is <i><u>smiling at</u></i>. What or who does he see that makes him smile/laugh? I can''t tell because we only have one half of the story. I do see that there are smiling people in the backdrop and that helps support the story that you are projecting with your title. <u>But</u> I think the photo would be far more stronger if you could show us who the gent is interacting with rather than the people behind him that he is not. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hi CNovak. Thank you! What was happening was, everybody was dancing to a rock band in Mill Valley California. The person to the left would have distracted and changed the balance of the shot. The main person is actually a lady and I thought her smile was simply beautiful and so genuine. She really was not interacting with anyone but rather just dancing happily...and now you know the rest of the story... :)</td>', 'Originally posted by CNovack: Voted earlier coming back to comment. Nice candid street photo. I like how you captured his beaming smile. However, I do wish that you captured more of what was ocurring on the left side of the frame to tell the story of what he is smiling at. What or who does he see that makes him smile/laugh? I can''t tell because we only have one half of the story. I do see that there are smiling people in the backdrop and that helps support the story that you are projecting with your title. But I think the photo would be far more stronger if you could show us who the gent is interacting with rather than the people behind him that he is not.   Hi CNovak. Thank you! What was happening was, everybody was dancing to a rock band in Mill Valley California. The person to the left would have distracted and changed the balance of the shot. The main person is actually a lady and I thought her smile was simply beautiful and so genuine. She really was not interacting with anyone but rather just dancing happily...and now you know the rest of the story... :)', '2012-08-20 03:19:15.000000', NULL, 0),
